---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/content/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
import { profilePageJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';

const path = '/about/';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path }];
const author = siteConfig.author;
const aboutUpdatedAt = '2026-11-25';
const jsonLd = [
  profilePageJsonLd({
    dateCreated: `${siteConfig.launchedAt}T00:00:00+05:00`,
    dateModified: `${aboutUpdatedAt}T00:00:00+05:00`,
  }),
];
const profileLinks = author.sameAs.filter(Boolean);
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`About ${siteConfig.siteName} – Free Document Generators`}
  description={`About ${siteConfig.siteName}: who builds these free browser-based business document generators, how the templates are made, and clear limits. Contact ${siteConfig.contactEmail}.`}
  path={path}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <h1>About {siteConfig.siteName}</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    {siteConfig.siteName} is a free set of niche business document generators—estimates, invoices,
    contracts, consent forms, and creative templates. Fill a form in the browser, preview the
    document, and export PDF or DOCX. Form inputs stay on your device.
  </p>
  <p class="content-meta byline">
    Last updated <time datetime={aboutUpdatedAt}>{aboutUpdatedAt}</time>
  </p>

  <h2 id="maintainer">Who builds this site</h2>
  <p>
    {siteConfig.siteName} is built and maintained by {author.name}. It is a one-person project, not a
    law firm, accounting practice, or licensed advisory service. The public launch baseline for this
    site is <time datetime={siteConfig.launchedAt}>{siteConfig.launchedAt}</time>.
  </p>
  {/* Owner: set PUBLIC_AUTHOR_BIO in Workers Builds / .env to replace the short bio below. */}
  <div id="personal-bio" class="author-bio">
    <h3>{author.name}</h3>
    <p>{author.shortBio}</p>
    <p>
      Day-to-day work on {siteConfig.siteName} means shipping fillable contractor and freelancer
      templates (estimates, invoices, change orders, photography and videography contracts, NDAs),
      citing primary public sources on each page, and keeping exports client-side so filled forms
      never hit a Docuklin server. Sister free-tool sites by the same maintainer are listed below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contact: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>
      {profileLinks.length > 0 && (
        <>
          {' '}
          · Profiles:{' '}
          {profileLinks.map((url, i) => {
            const label = /github\.com/i.test(url)
              ? 'GitHub'
              : /reddit\.com/i.test(url)
                ? 'Reddit'
                : /linkedin\.com/i.test(url)
                  ? 'LinkedIn'
                  : /(?:twitter|x)\.com/i.test(url)
                    ? 'X'
                    : 'Profile';
            return (
              <>
                {i > 0 && ' · '}
                <a href={url} rel="noopener noreferrer me">
                  {label}
                </a>
              </>
            );
          })}
        </>
      )}
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    There is no headshot here on purpose. This page does not invent credentials, expert titles, or
    stock photos. LinkedIn, X (Twitter), and a longer personal bio can be added via site config when
    the owner publishes those profiles—see <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> and deployment
    configuration docs.
  </p>

  <h2>How the templates are made</h2>
  <p>
    Each tool is a fillable form with a live preview and PDF/DOCX export. Educational copy cites
    public primary sources (for example IRS, SBA, Cornell LII, HUD, CDC, U.S. Copyright Office, FTC)
    listed at the bottom of the page. When a page shows a last-reviewed date, that is the day the
    maintainer last checked the copy against those sources—not a claim that the law is unchanged
    forever. Full process: <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It does not give legal, tax, or medical advice. Contract, invoice, and receipt pages are editable samples and bookkeeping aids.</li>
    <li>Your form inputs stay in your browser. Optional drafts use localStorage on your device. Analytics cookies are described on the <a href="/cookies/">cookie notice</a>.</li>
    <li>It is not affiliated with the IRS, SBA, HUD, CDC, FTC, or any brand named in examples.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
  <p>
    The site is free. Google Analytics is configured for aggregate traffic. Google AdSense may be
    enabled when the publisher flag is set. There are no affiliate links today.
  </p>

  <h2>Other free tool sites by the same maintainer</h2>
  <p>Listed here only, not in every footer:</p>
  <ul>
    {siteConfig.siblingSites.map((s) => (
      <li><a href={s.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.name}</a></li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with the page
    URL, what looks wrong, and a link to the source that shows the right information. Confirmed
    fixes are listed in the <a href="/methodology/#corrections">correction log</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .author-bio {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--brand, #0f6b5c);
    background: var(--surface, #f8faf9);
  }
  .author-bio h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .author-bio p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
